KZ3 patch 2045: the walker's per-stage counters, the srv_table memo, the per-list render-state memo
and sampled-units-only texture binds.
Counters (RSX_PERF=1 + RSX_PERF_PROF=A,B, off otherwise): `[perf-walk2]` per second inside the window: `meth` = time
inside the FIFO method loop per command group (draws and the write-backs they trigger included), the draw split
(pre, surf, texloop, desc with srvtbl/smptbl, rec with recent, post with rs = decode_render_state, bar = sampled-
surface barriers, omrt = OMSetRenderTargets block, memo hits); `[perf-redecode]`/`[perf-hash]`/`[perf-newtex]` when the window
closes: the textures re-decoded / hashed / newly cached inside it by source (top 16 by bytes); `[perf-flush]` per second: ld_flush
calls by reason (n/ms, the GPU wait included) and `tex-up` = the upload half (barriers + CopyTextureRegion) of the
texture refreshes.
srv_table memo (LD_NO_SRVTBL_MEMO=1 off): the last 32 (16-slot SRV table -> ring base) pairs; a hit returns the
ring table already holding those descriptors. g_srv_desc_gen advances at every SRV (re)write (ld_create_srv wraps
CreateShaderResourceView) and at every ring reset, so a hit never names stale descriptors or a recycled base.
Render-state memo (LD_NO_STATE_MEMO=1 off): OMSetRenderTargets, SetDescriptorHeaps, SetGraphicsRootSignature and
SetPipelineState are skipped when their arguments equal the last call on this command list; g_ld_sm_gen advances
at list Reset, at the compute paths (depth snapshot, host AA) and at every RTV/DSV descriptor write.
Sampled-units-only binds (LD_NO_UNIT_MASK_BIND=1 off): a texture unit the fragment program never samples (patch
2042's rsx_fp_texture_unit_mask) gets SRV_WHITE / SMP_DEFAULT instead of the stale texture and sampler left bound on
it: no lookup, no hash, and the 16-slot sampler table varies only with the sampled units, so the 128-table
shader-visible sampler ring (D3D12's 2,048-sampler heap limit) stops wrapping twice per frame (each wrap was a
descriptor-ring flush with a full GPU wait, 6.9 ms per frame).

From Project Helghast port/patches/2045-walker-stage-counters-srvtbl-state-memo.patch (KZ3's last ps3recomp v0.15.0 stack), imported by KZ2.
KZ2: rebased by hand (the new-entry ld_redecode_note sits before the decode, as in KZ3; 2039 lines absent).

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.18.0 (hand-merged): both sides kept (meth_t0 after upstream's fast path)

